# The two example directories swapped roles.
#
# `examples/` (plural) used to be ignored here, from when it was a scratch
# directory. It now holds examples/repo-review/, the composite-tool demo the
# README links to -- a flagship example git refuses to track is not one.
#
# `example/` (singular) is the pre-rebrand deployment scraps: nginx configs,
# pm2 configs, an oauth-server sketch, per-language curl demos. Local material,
# not part of what this project ships.
example/

nohup.out
.c9revisions/
.vscode/

# FileAuthProvider/SqliteAuthProvider default config -- may contain real
# API keys (or the auto-generated demo key), never meant to be committed.
# See lib/auth/ and README.md's Authentication section.
/auth.json
/auth.sqlite3

# Internal planning and review docs, kept locally by the maintainer only --
# see docs/design-decisions.md for the public-facing distillation of these.
#
# Deliberately NOT path-anchored. These were once written as
# /docs/<name>.md, which matches only the repo-root copy: a copy of one of
# them anywhere else (docs/verification-5.0.0/SPEC-REFACTOR-HANDOFF.md, which
# is exactly what happened and reached a public remote) sailed straight past
# the rule. Matching by basename means any copy, at any depth, is ignored.
cdif-audit-and-refactoring-plan.md
direct-peer-channels-design.md
PRE-RELEASE-AUDIT.md
ROADMAP-7.0.0.md
SPEC-REFACTOR-HANDOFF.md
v6-module-api-and-es6-design.md

# Build and scratch archives. `npm pack` drops its tarball in the repo root on
# every release rehearsal, and ad-hoc archives of working notes have landed in
# docs/ -- one of them was committed and pushed with a copy of a
# maintainer-local document inside it, which no .gitignore rule can catch once
# it is inside an archive.
#
# Deliberately not a bare `*.tgz`: pre-installed-packages/cdif-load-test-0.0.4.tgz
# is a test fixture that is meant to be tracked.
/countinghouse-*.tgz
docs/*.tgz
